# FUTURE QUARANTINED-CONSUMER INTEGRATION PROPOSAL — DO NOT APPLY
#
# The following is a design seam only, based on the R30 archive members pinned
# by R34. `machine.rs` and `receiving.rs` are UNKNOWN_WRITER/quarantined and
# were not read from the live checkout. The archive is streamed source evidence,
# not permission to edit those paths.
#
# Add `snapshot: HirSnapshotToken` to the test-only request-consumer,
# selected-installation, and callback-route evidence records. In
# `Machine::propagate_request`, obtain one token from
# `self.program.hir_snapshot_token()`, clone it into both selected-installation
# and request-consumer records, and pass a clone into
# `Receiving::callback_route_for_request`. Store that received token on each
# `CallbackRouteEvidence` produced for the request. Immediately before
# `callback_route_json` translates any HIR-relative coordinate, require
# `machine.program.hir_snapshot_token().identifies_same_snapshot(&consumer.snapshot)`,
# and require the selected-installation and callback-route tokens to match the
# same owner token. A mismatch returns a typed foreign-snapshot error before
# indexing the HIR declaration list.
#
# Replace the existing `expect`-based family/operation lookup in the future
# serializer integration with checked lookups: absent effect family,
# out-of-range effect index, absent operation, and out-of-range operation index
# all fail closed. Decode the entire permission-family vector with a fallible
# traversal that preserves order and length; any failed member rejects the
# whole row. Compare the decoded operations/families structurally with their
# R32 keys before applying coverage/round-trip facts.
#
# The opaque Rust capability intentionally has no Debug, numeric, spelling,
# or JSON representation here. This proposal shows owner attachment/checking
# at the Rust evidence boundary; transporting an authenticated owner capability
# to an offline certificate/Lean consumer requires a separately reviewed
# representation and remains OPEN. `selected_arm` remains a typed
# SourceNodeKey internally, while its existing Debug serialization is lossy and
# must not be treated as an arm identity.
